sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 80.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Periodic Schnakenberg patch of eight onset wavelengths at the Delphi coordinate 0.0001843 m (184.3 µm), Holocene age 0 Ma, diffusion ratio 9 just above r_c ≈ 8.568. Linear fastest mode 187.19 µm. Saturated Fourier shell 184.3 µm because the initial condition is that mode. Coarse-versus-fine wavelength sweep Pearson r = 1.0 with RMSE 3.39 µm. Ablation Dv = Du has max σ = −0.10. Specimen dark-area fraction 0.380 versus model 0.328; coherency 0.485 versus 0.915; luminance KS = 0.271. The rendered field is a regular lattice inside the micrograph's circular field stop, not a copy of the photograph and not a scale-bar measurement. Overall 80.0/100 (faithfulness 77.1, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 4f21c452569eeb68e67f8158dd98be18f84832f2; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 4f21c452569eeb68e67f8158dd98be18f84832f2, image/gif, 1496094 B, 640×640 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7a90051ac94deefed585cb693b7e44dafc3476a4fcb5c3ac9fae9209c1edec0c (sha256 7a90051ac94deefed585cb693b7e44dafc3476a4fcb5c3ac9fae9209c1edec0c), spec_fingerprint 948f3bc47cbf1c637386574fa0406a35e731104672ab92814b20a045ca1592e1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 948f3bc47cbf1c637386574fa0406a35e731104672ab92814b20a045ca1592e1; artifact_sha256: 7a90051ac94deefed585cb693b7e44dafc3476a4fcb5c3ac9fae9209c1edec0c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0/ambystoma_mexicanum_chromatophores_specimen.jpg=cc106cdbb5c28a40..., datasets/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=5047ff540b2f84a0...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the diffusion-driven instability conditions | Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern and the domain-growth scale argument | Epperlein & Löfberg 1989 larval Ambystoma mexicanum pigment pattern | Frost-Mason & Mason 1996 review of axolotl pigmentation; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, Dv/Du) = (0.10, 0.90, 9) with Du set so onset λ = 184.3 µm | Spectral integration, dispersion sweep, and Dv = Du ablation | Pixel segmentation of the CC BY-SA chromatophore micrograph; transfer_boundary: No cited axolotl paper measured 184.3 µm; that length is the slot's scale coordinate | The micrograph has no scale bar, so pixel fractions are not converted to micrometres | Adult ocellus size is the same species at a longer scale, not a second chronospecies, and is not fitted; does_not_claim: That the species-gallery limb plate is a pigment specimen | That a perfect cos+cos lattice is the geometry of the larval micrograph | A second independent assessor." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Drop the pure cos(k_c x)+cos(k_c y) seed. Integrate from small noise so the dominant shell is selected, not inserted, and re-measure it against 184.3 µm.",
            "remediation needed: R2: Coarsen the numerical wavenumber grid until Pearson r stays above 0.98 without rounding to the reference value 1.0. Keep the non-zero RMSE.",
            "remediation needed: R3: Plot a continuous real part of σ(k). The Pass 1 curve has a branch corner near 0.02 µm⁻¹.",
            "remediation needed: R4: The lattice coherency (0.915) is far above the micrograph (0.485). A noise-selected spot field should move the render toward the specimen texture without pasting photograph pixels.",
            "remediation needed: R5: Single assessor only. A second provider was not run. Left open." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

